## 7. Embedded Static Asset Serving & Air-Gapped Security (`src/assets.rs`)

### 7.1 Compile-Time Asset Embedding
Static files located in `crates/flightreader-server/assets/` are embedded into the compiled binary via `rust-embed 8.5`:

```rust
// src/assets.rs
use axum::{
    http::{header, HeaderValue, StatusCode, Uri},
    response::{IntoResponse, Response},
};
use rust_embed::RustEmbed;

/// Static assets embedded directly into the server binary at compile time.
#[derive(RustEmbed)]
#[folder = "assets/"]
pub struct EmbeddedAssets;
```

### 7.2 Strict Air-Gapped Content-Security-Policy (CSP)
To strictly enforce the zero-cloud invariant and prevent any DNS leaks, external font requests, or unauthorized telemetry tracking, all HTTP responses from `flightreader-server` inject the following authoritative CSP header:

```http
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data:; connect-src 'self' ws:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
```

### 7.3 Security Defense-in-Depth Headers
In addition to CSP, the server attaches:
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` (prevents MIME sniffing exploits).
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY` (prevents clickjacking attacks).
- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` (prevents path leakage).
- `Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()` (disables hardware sensors).

### 7.4 Static File Handler Implementation
```rust
pub async fn static_handler(uri: Uri) -> Response {
    let mut path = uri.path().trim_start_matches('/').to_string();

    // Default root and empty paths to index.html
    if path.is_empty() {
        path = "index.html".to_string();
    }

    match EmbeddedAssets::get(&path) {
        Some(content) => {
            let mime = mime_guess::from_path(&path).first_or_octet_stream();

            let mut response = (StatusCode::OK, content.data).into_response();
            let headers = response.headers_mut();

            // MIME type
            headers.insert(header::CONTENT_TYPE, HeaderValue::from_str(mime.as_ref()).unwrap());

            // Strict Air-Gap CSP Header
            headers.insert(
                header::HeaderName::from_static("content-security-policy"),
                HeaderValue::from_static(
                    "default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data:; connect-src 'self' ws:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'"
                ),
            );

            // Security Hardening Headers
            headers.insert(header::X_CONTENT_TYPE_OPTIONS, HeaderValue::from_static("nosniff"));
            headers.insert(header::X_FRAME_OPTIONS, HeaderValue::from_static("DENY"));
            headers.insert(header::HeaderName::from_static("referrer-policy"), HeaderValue::from_static("no-referrer"));

            response
        }
        None => {
            // If path has no extension, fall back to index.html for Single Page Application client routing
            if !path.contains('.') {
                if let Some(index) = EmbeddedAssets::get("index.html") {
                    let mut response = (StatusCode::OK, index.data).into_response();
                    let headers = response.headers_mut();
                    headers.insert(header::CONTENT_TYPE, HeaderValue::from_static("text/html; charset=utf-8"));
                    headers.insert(
                        header::HeaderName::from_static("content-security-policy"),
                        HeaderValue::from_static(
                            "default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data:; connect-src 'self' ws:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'"
                        ),
                    );
                    return response;
                }
            }

            (StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, "404 Not Found").into_response()
        }
    }
}
```

